    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Credit card statement</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Accounting</gui><gui>Credit card statement</gui></guiseq>
  checks a credit card account against the card company's statement, the way
  <link xref="bank_statement"/> does for a bank account.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Credit Card</gui>. Its <gui>Balance</gui> is
    shown, and every charge not yet reconciled is listed.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click the icon in the date box and choose the statement's closing
    date.</p></item>
    <item><p>Add any interest, fees or rewards the statement shows, and the
    payment, as below.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check <gui>R</gui> on each charge on the statement. The window
    menu has <gui>All reconciled on</gui> and <gui>All reconciled
    off</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Reconcile</gui>. If the date was already used for this
    card you are asked whether to use it again or choose another.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Click a charge's date or description to correct it.
  <gui>Refresh</gui> reloads the list, and <gui>Credit card statement
  history</gui> opens <link xref="credit_card_statement_history"/>.</p>

  <section id="fees">
  <title>Fees and rewards</title>
  <p>Under <gui>Fees and Rewards</gui>, type a description and the amount,
  choose the expense or income <gui>account</gui> it belongs to, and click
  <gui>Save</gui>. An expense account adds the amount to the card balance, as
  a fee or interest; an income account takes it off, as a reward.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="payment">
  <title>Paying the card</title>
  <p>Type the <gui>Payment of</gui> amount, choose the bank account it is
  paid <gui>from</gui>, type the <gui>transaction number</gui> and click
  <gui>Add</gui>. The payment moves the money from the bank to the
  card.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="options">
  <title>Window menu options</title>
  <p>Uncheck <gui>Save Reconciled rows to database</gui> to check charges off
  without saving the checks, for instance to try a total. <gui>Reconcile</gui>
  is then disabled. With <gui>Edit mode</gui> checked, which asks for the
  administrator password, right click a charge and choose <gui>Edit</gui> to
  correct the incoming invoice it came from; see <link
  xref="incoming_invoice_edit"/>.</p>
  </section>

</page>
